CORE
test.c
--nondet-volatile-write-model A:observe_A --nondet-volatile-write-model B:observe_B --mmio-weak --mmio-weak-depth 2
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
a write to A observed before GO: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
Deeper reordering: with a posted-write buffer of depth 2, both writes to A can
be outstanding when B is written, so the command can be observed before either
write to A. This reordering cannot be exhibited by a depth-1 buffer (see
depth1.desc), where the second write to A forces the first to be observed.
